{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob038_count15",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  clk\r\n - input  reset\r\n - output q (4 bits)\r\n\r\nThe module should implement a 4-bit binary counter that counts from 0\r\nthrough 15, inclusive, with a period of 16. Assume all sequential logic\r\nis triggered on the positive edge of the clock. The reset input is active\r\nhigh synchronous, and should reset the counter to 0.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "reset",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "q",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 4,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, single self-contained TopModule DUT; xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "2d538591-cc38-4a54-a4ca-20565b0bf0b5",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "1cbbf9ce-6bfa-4a84-a496-fbaaa226b8b8",
    "source_sha256": "c2dc7308d03949fe001bf60001cb48fbbab3ec689dbc22f80f24e191f317bd18",
    "source": "module TopModule(input clk, input reset, output reg [3:0] q); always @(posedge clk) if (reset) q <= 0; else q <= q + 2; endmodule\n"
  },
